## Railway deployment

### Option A — Docker Compose (Postgres included, no manual URL)

Deploy the repo using `docker-compose.yml`. Railway creates a Postgres service and backend automatically with `DATABASE_URL` wired in.

### Option B — Single backend service

If deploying only the root `Dockerfile`, you **must** also add a PostgreSQL plugin on Railway and reference its `DATABASE_URL`. Without it the container will fail at startup.

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Branch | `main` |
| Builder | Dockerfile (root) |

